1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,748
Does a lower rate mean this loan costs less? Let us compare fees
and insurance in TrueCost.

2
00:00:07,248 --> 00:00:22,795
We chose loan comparison from seven team ideas because the decision is financial.
Compare two offers as a guest, then sign in to save and revisit. These measures need validation.

3
00:00:23,295 --> 00:00:46,956
Two ten lakh rupee, ten year offers: Guest bank A at 8.50%, Guest bank B at 8.90%.
Fees, GST, insurance, and other charges use fresh draft defaults. These are synthetic figures.

4
00:00:47,456 --> 00:01:04,793
See the full breakdown estimates Effective APR, Monthly EMI, Cost per lakh, and Total cost.
I check the Recommendation, assumptions, and warnings.

5
00:01:05,293 --> 00:01:19,224
The first comparison is available to a guest. Saving or downloading requires an account.
I choose the save intent, with the result as the return target during verification.

6
00:01:19,724 --> 00:01:32,182
Saving requires account verification. This edit omits the sign-in screen for privacy.
Hosted evidence covers email verification; credentials stay out of view.

7
00:01:32,682 --> 00:01:48,174
The OTP is private, so this edit omits the code screen.
Hosted evidence records the check with synthetic data. No address, code, or inbox appears here.

8
00:01:48,674 --> 00:02:02,715
The original save request resumes after verification. I wait for Saved to your account.
I call it saved only after server acknowledgement and do not select Save again.

9
00:02:03,215 --> 00:02:15,407
I open Saved comparisons and choose Saved result.
This stored snapshot contains the recorded figures, fees, and warnings.

10
00:02:15,907 --> 00:02:36,873
The detail page shows recorded Effective APR, fees, and warnings.
I generate the PDF, wait for Your report is ready, then download it. Print this result is the fallback.

11
00:02:37,373 --> 00:03:00,683
TrueCost estimates from entered terms. The offers are synthetic.
This hosted development review uses development Clerk and Convex. Production pilot and operational readiness remain unproven.
